297
00:13:52,660 --> 00:13:55,760
A hundred sixty-five centimeters.

298
00:13:56,340 --> 00:13:58,300
He gave himself an extra centimeter.

299
00:13:58,640 --> 00:14:00,480
What's the highest reach you've ever gotten?

300
00:14:00,940 --> 00:14:02,900
Three hundred thirty-three centimeters high.

301
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:04,520
I win.

302
00:14:05,820 --> 00:14:08,200
What are you still doing down here, Karai?

303
00:14:08,460 --> 00:14:10,360
Game before ours is almost done.

304
00:14:10,360 --> 00:14:11,880
Oh well.

305
00:14:12,100 --> 00:14:12,580
See you later.

306
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:13,400
Yeah.

307
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:20,060
When Coach yells at you, leave me out of it.

308
00:14:20,300 --> 00:14:20,620
Whatever.

309
00:14:20,940 --> 00:14:22,620
I didn't want the grit shirt to sell out.

310
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:24,060
Uh, yeah, dude.

311
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:26,680
I'm pretty sure there's not much demand for that one.

312
00:14:27,020 --> 00:14:27,660
You don't know!

313
00:14:27,940 --> 00:14:29,440
Um, everybody knows.

314
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:32,280
Welcome back.

315
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:33,580
Where's Coach Yukai?

316
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:38,080
He got caught by some friends of his grandfather's, and he's still stuck talking to them.

317
00:14:38,360 --> 00:14:39,400
How are the matches going?

318
00:14:39,820 --> 00:14:41,240
One guy down there is awesome.

319
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:43,260
Kamo Medai's number five.

320
00:14:44,660 --> 00:14:45,540
Oh, here he is.

321
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:46,980
Karai Hoshiyumi.

322
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:48,860
169 centimeters.

323
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:49,320
Left!

324
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:49,860
Left!

325
00:14:49,860 --> 00:15:00,160
Oh, he actually hit over that block.

326
00:15:00,880 --> 00:15:02,700
That guy is a really good player, isn't he?

327
00:15:03,020 --> 00:15:04,660
Has he ever, like, been in a magazine?

328
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:05,580
Not yet.

329
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:08,120
Apparently he absolutely hates doing interviews.

330
00:15:08,820 --> 00:15:09,240
Really?

331
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:09,360
Really?

332
00:15:09,720 --> 00:15:13,960
I think I'd be super excited to do an interview, even if it was just for the school paper.

333
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:16,280
Hmm?

334
00:15:17,100 --> 00:15:18,380
Where are you going now?

335
00:15:19,860 --> 00:15:21,240
To watch from up close.

336
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:23,020
Karai!

337
00:15:28,020 --> 00:15:30,040
Stuffed like a pan-fried pork dumpling!

338
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,340
Could you see that block?

339
00:15:32,160 --> 00:15:33,340
He is on fire!

340
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:35,320
The kid is looking real good.

341
00:15:42,160 --> 00:15:42,720
Again?

342
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:43,800
Wow!

343
00:15:44,980 --> 00:15:46,500
That kid can do anything.

344
00:15:46,500 --> 00:15:50,040
Who is that number five?

345
00:15:58,200 --> 00:16:00,220
We have ourselves a service-ace!

346
00:16:00,300 --> 00:16:00,840
Hot dog!

347
00:16:01,500 --> 00:16:02,840
Hoshiyumi does it again!

348
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:04,580
He's a force to be reckoned with!

349
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:07,460
This pint-sized one-man army is on a roll, Joe!

350
00:16:07,460 --> 00:16:13,480
He is indeed, he is truly, the Tiny Giant Incarnate!

351
00:16:18,860 --> 00:16:20,020
Oh, wow.

352
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:27,740
You know, guys, Hinata's gone up against a two-meter Titan without batting an eye.

353
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:33,020
But now here's someone with his same height disadvantage, and he's already reaching his full potential.

354
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:36,300
That might be a pretty big shock to his psyche.

355
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:38,640
Just a random thought.

356
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:50,360
Hoshiyumi, wait up!

357
00:16:51,640 --> 00:16:53,160
You are amazing out there.

358
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:55,040
Congratulations on your win.

359
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:57,000
Oh, thank you very much.

360
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:04,140
The team's average height was 180 centimeters, which means that essentially every one of their players was quite a bit taller than you.

361
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:05,360
What was that like?

362
00:17:05,660 --> 00:17:06,580
That's not good.

363
00:17:06,840 --> 00:17:07,100
Huh?

364
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:10,880
He hates questions like, how can you play when you're so small?

365
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:12,480
Or what's it like to be short?

366
00:17:12,560 --> 00:17:13,780
Or is the game too tall?

367
00:17:14,540 --> 00:17:20,860
For as long as I've known him, whenever he pulls off a badass play, people tell him, you're such an amazing player for someone so small.

368
00:17:20,860 --> 00:17:24,120
And he tells them, I'm an amazing player, period.

369
00:17:24,660 --> 00:17:29,340
Compared to the rest of the world, 180 centimeters is actually on the shorter side, right?

370
00:17:29,900 --> 00:17:31,040
Uh, the world?

371
00:17:32,040 --> 00:17:34,900
Are you only interviewing me because I'm a short person?

372
00:17:35,480 --> 00:17:37,860
Oh, well, um...

373
00:17:39,040 --> 00:17:46,140
But the main thing that Karai hates most in the whole world is to be told that the reason he lost is because he's so short.

374
00:17:46,140 --> 00:17:53,440
Everyone is too obsessed with this idea that being short means you should give up on everything.

375
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:56,360
Look, my height is what it is.

376
00:17:56,720 --> 00:18:01,720
It may be a bit of a disadvantage in a volleyball game, but it does not make me helpless!

377
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:21,060
Okay, okay, I'm sorry about that.

378
00:18:21,220 --> 00:18:23,560
He can be a bit, well, difficult at times.

379
00:18:23,620 --> 00:18:24,520
Now I'm difficult?

380
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:27,360
All she was trying to do was give you a compliment.

381
00:18:27,780 --> 00:18:30,540
You said yourself that your height puts you at a disadvantage.

382
00:18:30,540 --> 00:18:34,780
Like it or not, it's still amazing that you're helping the team win despite that disadvantage.

383
00:18:35,080 --> 00:18:36,540
You're too self-conscious, man.

384
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:40,600
Well, maybe you need to learn how to sugarcoat things sometimes!

385
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:41,320
Sure.

386
00:18:41,640 --> 00:18:42,340
Now go on.

387
00:18:42,460 --> 00:18:43,660
